From 2e946d3dfc6b46b5173643f66e5eb221173a3d26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yun Dou <dixyes@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:32:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] arm64: Share what the emulations of the undefined
 instructions need

The emulation of the RCpc acquire loads replaces the instruction a task
was stopped on, reports a fault it cannot resolve at the address the
instruction would have used, and answers for the alignment the
architecture requires of the access. Emulating the LSE atomics needs the
same three things, so they are moved into a file of their own.

The RCpc loads behave exactly as before: the same page is written the same
way, the same signal is delivered for the same address, and the feature
register the alignment is read from is still read once at boot.

Assisted-by: dsh:DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash
(cherry picked from commit 423ebea2e866187cb383b4a065aabd63e77f30cd)
